{"name":"Painted Ash","hex":"#ddba8f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"painted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of paint"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Coated with paint.","Depicted in paint."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/painted"},{"term":"ash","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Abishira."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The solid remains of a fire.","The nonaqueous remains of a material subjected to any complete oxidation process."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paint","blocks":[{"text":"Paint is a material or mixture of colored liquid that, when applied to a solid material and allowed to dry, adds a film-like layer. As art, this is used to create an image or images known as a painting. Paint can be made in many colors and types. Most paints are either oil-based or water-based, and each has distinct characteristics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Multicolored_tempera_paints.jpg/330px-Multicolored_tempera_paints.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paint","wikidata":"Q174219"},{"title":"Ash","blocks":[{"text":"Ash is the solid remnants of fires. Specifically, ash refers to all non-aqueous, non-gaseous residues that remain after something burns. In analytical chemistry, to analyse the mineral and metal content of chemical samples, ash is the non-gaseous, non-liquid residue after complete combustion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Wood_ash.jpg/330px-Wood_ash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ash","wikidata":"Q152079"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Lascaux%2C_Megaloceros.jpg/500px-Lascaux%2C_Megaloceros.jpg?utm_sou